From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nathan Sanchez <nathanasanchez@google.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:55:55 +0000
Subject: [Vulkan] Sleep after device lost on certain GPUs

This mimics the similar approach taken in Dawn
(https://dawn-review.git.corp.google.com/c/dawn/+/314796/) where we
sleep for 1ms after vkQueueSubmit or vkQueueWaitIdle

Bug: 580857377
Change-Id: I9811a29ffccc0b30402ee77ec78872fb58525283
Reviewed-on: https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/1414538
Auto-Submit: Nathan Sanchez <nathanasanchez@google.com>
Commit-Queue: Nathan Sanchez <nathanasanchez@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Michael Ludwig <michaelludwig@google.com>
Commit-Queue: Michael Ludwig <michaelludwig@google.com>

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y): VulkanCommandBuffer::waitUntilFinished on this branch has no VK_TIMEOUT retry loop and used VULKAN_CALL_ERRCHECK; it is changed to VULKAN_CALL_RESULT (which logs and calls checkVkResult exactly as before) so the VkResult is available for the new sleepAfterLostDeviceWait() check. GrVkGpu.cpp keeps this branch's include list plus <numeric>/<thread>.

diff --git a/src/gpu/ganesh/vk/GrVkCaps.cpp b/src/gpu/ganesh/vk/GrVkCaps.cpp
index 6f9a17c48dc8a2a3fe9b5dba9a6faf723c64564d..0d7c44126d17748ceff1ec31460cc61a033af09b 100644
--- a/src/gpu/ganesh/vk/GrVkCaps.cpp
+++ b/src/gpu/ganesh/vk/GrVkCaps.cpp
@@ -519,6 +519,14 @@ void GrVkCaps::applyDriverCorrectnessWorkarounds(const VkPhysicalDevicePropertie
         fShouldAlwaysUseDedicatedImageMemory = true;
     }
 
+    const skgpu::DriverVersion driverVersion = skgpu::ParseVulkanDriverVersion(
+            VK_DRIVER_ID_ARM_PROPRIETARY, properties.driverVersion);
+    if (skgpu::kARM_VkVendor == properties.vendorID &&
+        driverVersion >= skgpu::DriverVersion(42, 0) &&
+        driverVersion < skgpu::DriverVersion(56, 0)) {
+        fSleepAfterLostDeviceWait = true;
+    }
+
     // On Mali galaxy s7 and s9 we see lots of rendering issues with image filters dropping out when
     // using only primary command buffers. We also see issues on the P30 running android 28.
     if (skgpu::kARM_VkVendor == properties.vendorID && androidAPIVersion <= 28) {
